{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210679-sun-forged-oath-an-ex3-chronicle","id":1210679,"title":"Sun Forged Oath: An EX3 Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T16:43:33-07:00","id":1210679,"title":"Sun Forged Oath: An EX3 Chronicle","content":"Hello friends! I wanted to share with you the Obsidian Portal for my newest EX3 Chronicle Sun Forged Oath. Its a sequel/spin-off to my first EX3 game <a href=\"https://hakura-chronicle.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Hakura Chronicle</a>. Last night the mortal heroes of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1198240-talk-about-your-locations\">Township of Tenyio</a> just had the first of their companions undergo the Second Breath as a Solar exalted! So I felt it was an auspicious time to share it with all of you fine folks here on the Forums.Most of this group has never played Exalted before and they are loving it. I hope you will enjoy checking out the world building and adventures we are engaging in on Obsidian Portal:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","user":"Keichiokami","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T12:25:39-07:00","id":1215571,"title":"","content":"So my players came together and in a collaborative effort, did a three-die stunt of Establishing A Fact about the Inn/Tavern in the Township of Tenyio that is their home base. its weird, creative, and so thoroughly the kind of rich mystical strangeness I feel embodies Exalted: <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Mysteries of the Fox &amp; Hound Inn</span></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">There was a consistent system used to bring in new Hounds to work for Subdued Summer at the Fox and Hound Inn. First, Autumn Tempest, the Houndmaster, would set her sights on a potential candidate. This individual must be both a loyal vault of secrets and a ready voice of reason. They must possess a keen nose for danger and the ability to fight whatever that danger may be. They must be a friend to Subdued Summer \u2013 who can not tolerate the notion of solitude. And, finally, they must show a healthy fear of the nearby presence of a door in the basement of every Fox and Hound Inn \u2013 one emblazoned with a cedar tree and humming with unfamiliar energy. This final requirement on Tempest\u2019s list was tested at the conclusion of every interview. Any individual who could walk down the basement steps and not feel a chill down their spine was immediately disqualified without explanation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Radiant Koi had met and exceeded every requirement. Summer had been pleased, as there was a new inn opening shortly in Tenyio and she did not feel like the Fox without a Hound to assist her in day to day tasks. Summer and Koi became fast friends, and the pair developed the habit of having drinks together late into the evenings at least once a week.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It was during one of those first long talks that Radiant Koi asked about the magic in the tavern. The question wasn\u2019t an unexpected one \u2013 every Hound asks Summer about it eventually. Most take their time in finding the courage to ask; the words lost behind some combination of primal fear and the suspicion that the answer may be more uncomfortable than the mystery of the place. Koi, as expected, overcame his trepidation in record time.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u201cSo.. what\u2019s the deal here? The basement creeps me out,\u201d he said, taking a long draw of his pipe.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Summer arched an eyebrow and sat a moment, considering. \u201cOnce I tell you, this becomes your home. Quitting or leaving are no longer options. Are you prepared for that?\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Koi nodded then, and the confidence he had in his decision was palpable. \u201cYes. Tell me.\u201d At that, Subdued Summer walked towards the door to the basement and waited expectantly for Koi to follow, which he did after swiftly knocking back the remainder of his glass.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">They stood in front of a large, solid door. To the casual observer it, like the inn it resided in, was unremarkable. It stood eight feet tall and was made of solid cedar which had been stained a deep red. A tree was burned into the wood at its center, the branches of which stretched across the surface, reaching towards the sky. Summer reached into one of her many pockets and removed what appeared to be a piece of leather cord. She handed it to Koi and took a step back. Another test.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u201cYou may not see it, but this door has a lock. I\u2019m sure you can find it.\u201d Inspecting the cord in his hand, Koi realized there was a pendant \u2013 a small, green leaf which seemed to be carved with some skill out of some type of wood. He sighed, a symptom of impatience and drink, and set to work finding the so-called lock. After what felt like hours he discovered it: one of the leaves of the tree had a subtly different texture than the others. On a whim, Koi pressed the leaf into the indentation in question and was rewarded.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The cedar tree on the door seemed to come alive before his eyes. Subtle color manifested itself in the burned lines, green leaves seemed to move in some gentle summer breeze, and Koi was sure he could hear the branches rustling against one another for a moment. As quickly as it began, the illusion had ceased and the door split cleanly down the middle. The newly transformed entrance opened inward, revealing what could only be described as a lush grotto.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">At the center of the room Radiant Koi and Subdued Summer now stood in was a tree which perfectly mirrored the living illusion on the door. It stood impossibly tall, reaching a height that would, under normal circumstances, be causing its branches to breach the floor of the tavern itself. Spiraling outward from the trunk was an intricate root system, each major vein leading towards a pair of double doors which resembled perfectly those found at the entrance of every Fox and Hound Inn. A pale, ethereal lavender light bathed every surface, and the sounds of the tavern \u2013 easily heard just outside the threshold- were eerily absent. Summer waited, giving Koi time to absorb and come to terms with what he was seeing. Once he was ready, she began.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u201cI grew up in Nexus, as you know. What you may not know, though, is that my father is Singed Wing of Dawn \u2013 yes, the very same \u2013 and my mother is a Haltan woman known as Oft Dreaming Lily. They loved each other once, I imagine, but soon came to quite the disagreement when it came to how I should be raised and educated. My mother wanted me to embrace my roots and help my people in their never ceasing war. My father wanted me to forge my own path. You can see what I tried to choose.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As a child, I primarily stayed with my father in the Bastion district of Nexus. Occasionally, Lily would decide motherhood suited her once more, and I\u2019d be whisked away to Halta for some gathering or training or other important milestone she\u2019d decided to foist upon me. The last time I saw her was my fifteenth name day. We\u2019d had an incredible fight over things i won\u2019t get into now, and she gave me a satchel made of the softest silk I had ever felt. Lily said it was time to choose \u2013 that she\u2019d be waiting for me on the day I decided to live with my \u2018true\u2019 family. And then she left, my half-sister in tow.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The satchel was filled with seeds from what some Haltan tribes refer to as their home tree. Trees are as important as air in that country \u2013 they are the definition of safety, because any who fall beneath the shelter of the canopy are food for the fae. The home tree is the one in which you\u2019re born and the one here, in this room, apparently grew from the seed of mine.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Now, that\u2019s not to imply all seeds of this nature result in sorcery like this. It\u2019s true that animals and plants in Halta grow to exceed expectations, probably because of nefarious dealings made with the faeries, but something like this simply should not have happened under normal circumstances. And yet, here we are!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Anyway. Lily gave me this sad satchel of seeds and went home. I threw the thing in a drawer and didn\u2019t think of it for the next three years until I was moving out of Father\u2019s estate. Keep them in mind, will you? They\u2019re the first puzzle piece in this situation we find ourselves in.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Another piece in this culmination of magic and timing is my father\u2019s family. Singed Wing of Dawn is, as most know, a sorcerer. He posses an extra bit of magic, though, that he\u2019s never been truly forthright about \u2013 something in the blood, you see? As far as I can ascertain, that bit of \u2018extra\u2019 is common in most generations of this family. Sometimes it\u2019s impressive, sometimes it isn\u2019t, and sometimes it doesn\u2019t show up at all \u2013 but it isn\u2019t always tied to sorcery.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Father or, at least, his family own quite a bit of property in Nexus. One of those parcels of land eventually became the original Fox and Hound, but when I was growing up I just knew it as my great uncle Dove of Morning\u2019s winter house. He\u2019d show up every year just ahead of Calibration and stay there until spring \u2013 said he wanted to be near his favorite niece during the holidays, and that he had important work to do. I\u2019m still not entirely sure what that work was \u2013 all I know is one morning he was there, and the next he was gone. His house was a burned out shell and no one would tell me why. I\u2019m still searching for specifics to this day \u2013 we never found a body.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I used to hide there, in the ruins, when I was sad or angry or needed to be alone. I still liked to be alone in those days. Fewer ghosts at my heels. Sometimes Autumn was with me \u2013 she\u2019d been just like family even in those days. So, when I turned 18, Father gave me the land and a blank check to do what I wanted with it. I decided to honor the memories granted me by my late uncle and sought to create a home for strangers at the holidays. He used to call me Little Kit, and Autumn Tempest was, to him, a loyal hound who made friends with one she was meant to chase.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The early days of planning weren\u2019t easy. I struggled to balance the embarrassment I feel to this day with a yearning to be accepted by my mother\u2019s family. And so, in designing the inn, I made some choices \u2013 irises, a saying from Father\u2019s family written in forest tongue, that kind of thing. And one last touch: a single seed from satchel Lily had given me. That piece of home felt important and I\u2019m not one to question my own intuition, so, I surreptitiously placed the seed in the exact center of the foundation of the inn. The spot held a vast amount of energy and my nerves were singing with it after I completed what I understand now was some sort of ritual.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Once the Nexus Fox and Hound was completed, I did my final tour with Autumn, as one does, to make sure everything was as planned. And it was, except for one thing: this room. There was a door which was certainly not included in the plans, just like the one you unlocked for me today. We couldn\u2019t get it open and believe me, we tried everything. Hammers, saws, fire \u2013 you name it. That is, until we built the second inn.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I placed another seed in the foundation of the next one \u2013 and why not? It seemed like a safe enough tradition to that point. Autumn and I again did the walkthrough, as we always do, although this time we brought Dierdre along. There it was again \u2013 the same door, in the exact same spot. We tried again to open it and it seemed to react when the satchel of seeds hovered near it. On a whim, Dierdre took one and placed it into the odd leaf \u2013 just as you did today, although it\u2019s different on every door, and the thing opened to this place.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">No, not a copy of this room \u2013 to this actual space. Each inn has a doorway which leads to this place. I can meet with other Hounds and conduct business within these walls \u2013 although if anyone besides myself spends too much time here, they come down with what can only be described as a short lived flu. The symptoms become worse if the person in question visits more than an hour or two a month \u2013 that seems to be the balance which needs to be struck.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The other thing is the doors here. Each time I open a new inn, another set grows from the root system and a portal is created here. They all lead to different inns \u2013 you can tell which one by counting the irises in each cluster on the stained glass panels. It\u2019s terribly convenient, until it isn\u2019t. If you were to walk through that set there, you\u2019d be in Nexus in what is, in reality, about five minutes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Time feels different, though, in the spaces between. It\u2019s easy to get lost \u2013 especially if you don\u2019t have that key with you to prove you are allowed to be travel there. When you first enter \u2013 and you will, all Hounds do eventually \u2013 you may be greeted by a spirit known as Rain\u2019s Cadence. She\u2019s friendly, for the most part, but she expects favors in exchange for her guidance and companionship. I think she may be a relative of mine, or at least friends of a relative, as she occasionally makes requests or asks questions revolving around my family. I have my suspicions she may be in contact with Oft Dreaming Lily \u2013 so whatever you do, be careful what you tell her. And don\u2019t make her any promises you can\u2019t or won\u2019t keep \u2013 I made that mistake once and was sick in bed for weeks. If it wasn\u2019t for Resplendent Jade Elixir, I may very well have died for my foolishness.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Cadence likes unique stones and exotic, aromatic herbs and teas. I\u2019d make a note of that, if I were you \u2013 often she\u2019s happy enough with those offerings to forget about her other requests. I worry one day she\u2019ll ask me for a great favor by way of one of you \u2013 so, please, use the portals sparingly and let me know when you do so.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> And don\u2019t ever speak of the key or this room to anyone else. It\u2019s one rule there is never an acceptable reason to break. Any questions?\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Radiant Koi had several, and once he seemed satisfied, Summer stretched and stood. Cunning Bite echoed her movements at her feet. \u201cLet\u2019s get a drink, shall we?\u201d</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","user":"Keichiokami","date":".  Formatting so it can be easier to read. 05-05-2018, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T02:10:24-07:00","id":1233642,"title":"","content":"So my players have done it again! They are now writing fully detailed summaries, recaps, out-of-session lore, and transcripts of in between sesion character interactions. The adventure log is now flooded with content. We will be celebrating 20 sessions (not including our five Side story sessions), this upcoming Sunday. Please celebrate with us by reading some of our recaps and if you have an Obsidian Portal account please become a Fan of our page! ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:40:23-07:00","id":1239591,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> Read the whole thing. Wished some sections weren't missing. Whatever happened with the Anhule that seemed to like Eagle Wind? I gather it was somehow connected to the fire? I saw later on it mentioned Low Vice battling an Anhule....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:54:41-07:00","id":1239595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210679-sun-forged-oath-an-ex3-chronicle?p=1239591#post1239591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> Read the whole thing. Wished some sections weren't missing. Whatever happened with the Anhule that seemed to like Eagle Wind? I gather it was somehow connected to the fire? I saw later on it mentioned Low Vice battling an Anhule....</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Yeah that session has not been fully recapped but I am more than happy to share what happened.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">So Bloodied Spindle, the Anhule that became infatuated with Eagle Wind, was eventually slain by Low Vice after consulting with Eagle Wind on how to approach the situation. It was agreed by Summer, Low Vice, and Eagle Wind that Bloodied Spindle may be the one responsible for reporting the secret of the portals and the sorcerous working that connected all the Fox &amp; Hound Inns together. Eagle Wind wanted to free the demon from Seven Season's Widow's service and the most expedient way they could come up with was slaying the demon and sending it back to the demon city, thus severing her contract with the death-knight. So the hunting down and slaying of Bloodied Spindle was green-lit and after the demon was slain, Low Vice re-summoned her (since he had the demon's name) and bound Bloodied Spindle into service and commanded her to serve Eagle Wind. So it was a happy ending, of sorts. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Glad you have become invested in the story, my players will be incredibly excited to hear some one is enjoying their recaps. ^_^</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:04:15-07:00","id":1239606,"title":"","content":"OK, just making sure I am 100% on-page:<br /> This resulted in the SAME Bloodied Spindle, memories intact, emotion intact, ending up with Eagle Wind? I'm not up on the new edition yet, so don't have my usual comprehensive lore base yet. Killing the Anhule just bounced it back to Malfeas, cut ties to the Widow, and boomeranged the Anhule back into Creation a wee-bit later with an &quot;ouch, temp-dying wasn't fun&quot; headache, happy ending for all concerned?<br /> <br /> BTW, that was an...unfortunate take on the Agatae lore. Agatae are basically my &quot;If there is a species of First Circle Demon I could set free in Creation, without giving SWLIHN some sort of malignant foothold, it'd be the Beauteous Wasps. Their motivation is just &quot;Want to be the best mount I can be, fly summoners to see cool real estate. As far as &quot;volatile&quot; demon warning-stories, I could think of about ten I'd go with ahead of the Agatae. The Amphylkea (know I mangled that name, the lizard-looking ones who adore soap bubbles, and go ape-shit collect all shadows and go shadow-monster if they hear a child's laughter), they'd be my choice for &quot;Demon not to fall in love with.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-28-2018, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T18:15:01-07:00","id":1239859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210679-sun-forged-oath-an-ex3-chronicle?p=1239606#post1239606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, just making sure I am 100% on-page:<br /> This resulted in the SAME Bloodied Spindle, memories intact, emotion intact, ending up with Eagle Wind? I'm not up on the new edition yet, so don't have my usual comprehensive lore base yet. Killing the Anhule just bounced it back to Malfeas, cut ties to the Widow, and boomeranged the Anhule back into Creation a wee-bit later with an &quot;ouch, temp-dying wasn't fun&quot; headache, happy ending for all concerned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is exactly how it went down. I love how humorously you have restated the events. ^_^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210679-sun-forged-oath-an-ex3-chronicle?p=1239606#post1239606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> BTW, that was an...unfortunate take on the Agatae lore. Agatae are basically my &quot;If there is a species of First Circle Demon I could set free in Creation, without giving SWLIHN some sort of malignant foothold, it'd be the Beauteous Wasps. Their motivation is just &quot;Want to be the best mount I can be, fly summoners to see cool real estate. As far as &quot;volatile&quot; demon warning-stories, I could think of about ten I'd go with ahead of the Agatae. The Amphylkea (know I mangled that name, the lizard-looking ones who adore soap bubbles, and go ape-shit collect all shadows and go shadow-monster if they hear a child's laughter), they'd be my choice for &quot;Demon not to fall in love with.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The player of Low Vice is a delightfully creative individual, its a pleasure to run for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T19:29:04-07:00","id":1239876,"title":"","content":"::nods:: I have to say, as a Storyteller, I've always experienced a preponderance of &quot;Most Creative Players = Most likely to be the players with PCs deeply involved with sorcery or necromancy.&quot; Storytelling arcs like &quot;Yeah, let's steal a Demon&quot; are a joy. You see where I described my first Storytelling of a PC summoning a Third Circle Demon, above. That scene is one of my Top 3 Storytelling Moments.<br /> <br /> Logistically, do you find it difficult having more than one PC deeply into sorcery at once? I've had differing experiences, and I'm curious. Most of my Storytelling challenges tended to emerge as the PCs progressed in power. Not so much talking about mechanics, so much as the sorcerers capabilities taking things in an unexpected direction surprisingly fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:17:31-07:00","id":1239893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210679-sun-forged-oath-an-ex3-chronicle?p=1239876#post1239876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Logistically, do you find it difficult having more than one PC deeply into sorcery at once? I've had differing experiences, and I'm curious. Most of my Storytelling challenges tended to emerge as the PCs progressed in power. Not so much talking about mechanics, so much as the sorcerers capabilities taking things in an unexpected direction surprisingly fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, mostly because each initiation is different and the needs and desires of each PC are different regarding what they want out of Sorcery. I am never caught off guard regarding solutions to problems because I build all my plots with Workings in mind when I construct them. My plots tend to be presented with a sense of urgency. This urgency often males the PCs feel that using a Working to solve the problem involves an element of risk they often do not want to take. So they find more direct solutions to accomplish their goals rather than always relying on the Arcane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T00:44:16-07:00","id":1240748,"title":"","content":"New updates! More recaps of past sessions and the most current session involving Marita. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}